///1LOAD
Help by Willem Aandewiel
LOAD - Convert an Intel HEX file into a COM file

///2SYNTAX
  E>A:LOAD DEMO

LOAD reads DEMO.HEX and creates DEMO.COM.
Omit the .HEX extension in this command.

///2EXAMPLE
  E>A:ASM DEMO
  E>A:LOAD DEMO
  E>DEMO

First correct every assembly error reported by ASM.
LOAD creates the executable. Typing DEMO actually starts it.

///2FORMATS
Use LOAD for absolute Intel HEX output from ASM or MAC.
Use LINK for a .REL module produced by RMAC.
An existing .COM file does not need to be processed by LOAD again.
Successful conversion does not verify the program's logic.
